  "note": "Annual election of one third (five seats), Monday 15 January 1912, for the places of the members elected in 1909 (MacGeagh, Mahaffy, Waite, Drennan and Breen). Declared at 10.30 p.m. \"Of the 2,427 voters on the register, 1,652 polled. There were nine spoiled votes and one tendered vote.\" The Lurgan Times labels the candidates U. (Unionist), N. (Nationalist) and L. (Labour); it found the Nationalist George McGhee's fourth place \"not a little surprising\". The Lurgan Mail adds that 1,193 polled in 1906, 775 in 1907, 804 in 1908, 1,539 in 1909 and 1,210 in 1911."
